# Signing material — generated locally per SIGNING.md / ANDROID.md, never
# committed. GitHub Actions gets these as base64-encoded repo secrets, not
# files. This backstop exists in case any of it ever ends up inside your
# project directory instead of a scratch folder outside it.
*.p12
*.key
*.cer
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
*.keystore
*.jks
*_base64.txt

# Common local cruft
.DS_Store
node_modules/
